     real link with a given bandwidth.  The “fast” mode allows certain packets
     to bypass the dduummmmyynneett scheduler (if packet flow does not exceed pipe's
     bandwidth).  This is the reason why the “fast” mode requires less CPU cy‐
     cles per packet (on average) and packet latency can be significantly
     lower in comparison to a real link with the same bandwidth.  The default
     mode is “normal”.  The “fast” mode can be enabled by setting the
